1854 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Nortel Institute for Telecommunications \050NIT\051 was originally established in 1997 with funding from the Nortel Networks Corporation\056 The institute included 10 open\055research labs across the UofT campus\056\240\n\240\nIn 1999\054 the institute received funding from Canada Foundation for Innovation \050CFI\051\054 Ontario Research and Development Challenge Fund \050ORDCF\051 and the  Ontario Innovation Trust \050OIT\051\054 which collectively funded the design and construction of the Prototyping Cleanroom in the Bahen Building\056 The cleanroom officially opened in May 2003\056\240The institute was re\055named the Emerging Communications Technology Institute \050ECTI\051 in 2005\054 after the amalgamation of the Nortel Institute and the Micro Fabrication Research Laboratory in the Pratt Building\056 \n\nIn 2005\054 CFI funding obtained to construct an Electron Beam Nanolithography Facility in the basement of the Wallberg Building\054 as well as purchase a state\055of\055the\055art Electron Beam Lithography tool\056 The Wallberg Nanolithography Facility was officially available to academic and industrial users in September 2009\056\240\n\240\nThe institute was re\055branded as the Toronto Nanofabrication Centre \050TNFC\051 in April 2013\056\240)
     /K [ 39 ]
     /P 1855 0 R
     /Pg 1776 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

